<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's Daehan buys 24,500 tonnes of U.S. wheat.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's Daehan buys 24,500 tonnes of U.S. wheat.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Daehan Flour Mills Co Ltd on Friday said it bought 24,500 tonnes of U.S. No.1 wheat from Japanese trading house Marubeni Corp.</p>
<p>A Daehan official said shipment was set for May 1-30 to the western port of Inchon.  </p>
<p>The official said the total amount would be split into four postions -- 11,000 tonnes of western white/soft white, 1,000 tonnes of western white (protein minimum 10 percent), 2,000 tonnes of hard red winter (protein minimum 11.5 percent), and 10,500 tonnes of dark northern spring (protein minimum 14 percent).</p>
<p>Details for the results are as follow:</p>
<p>  Type of Wheat		   Tonne	Price/T (FOB)</p>
<p>  Western White/Soft White   11,000	 $154.32</p>
<p>  Western White		   1,000	 $157.63</p>
<p>  Hard Red Winter		 2,000	 $182.80</p>
<p>  Dark Northern Spring	 10,500	 $187.58</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
</text>
